b237468a-3130-4019-b281-032b0ab34e65	Komal	7045817502	\N	Female	\N	\N	I am currently doing articleship at pwc and I am constantly thinking that will i be able to complete my lectures, I also don't like sitting late in the office as I feel that if we can complete the work during the office hours why wait late, I also want to live my life outside the office. I have seen people in the team that i was a part of earlier coming late then sitting late to complete the work but why should I do it, I come on time and I dont want to stay that late so what's wrong. Now I am temporarily part of a new team and I have heard from my friend already working in that team that they stay late till like 1 to 2 at night. I don't want to work with them and I really dont want they I stay with the team for a long time or become a permanent member. During office hours, I miss my family and the time that I have spent with them. I usually dont go out much and all that but now it feels as if will I be stuck there.	answered	I have also gone through similar experiences in my life. There have been difficult times, moments when tears would well up in my eyes, too.\nBut with time, I realised something beautiful, look at how beautifully those very experiences have shaped me!\n\nThink of a sculptor carving a murti. With every tak-tak of the chisel, the stone undergoes force and pain. But when the carving is complete, the murti looks incredibly beautiful.\nSimilarly, the Universe sends different situations into our lives. Each situation chisels us, shapes us, and helps us become a better version of ourselves.\n\nSo, whenever you go through difficult times, don't just look at the pain you are experiencing. Look at the person you are becoming through it. Consider it a boon from the Universe. Perhaps, through every challenge, the Universe is simply chiselling you into something even more beautiful.\n\n        ~ Muniraj Shri MuktiMandan Vijayji MS	2026-10-28 04:43:50.721012+00	2026-10-17 06:53:38.202111+00	1009	SUxKLVExMDA5	[{"id": "df675a4b-c86a-41f0-acfe-e1f4c46b3be2", "text": "I am currently doing articleship at pwc and I am constantly thinking that will i be able to complete my lectures, I also don't like sitting late in the office as I feel that if we can complete the work during the office hours why wait late, I also want to live my life outside the office. I have seen people in the team that i was a part of earlier coming late then sitting late to complete the work but why should I do it, I come on time and I dont want to stay that late so what's wrong. Now I am temporarily part of a new team and I have heard from my friend already working in that team that they stay late till like 1 to 2 at night. I don't want to work with them and I really dont want they I stay with the team for a long time or become a permanent member. During office hours, I miss my family and the time that I have spent with them. I usually dont go out much and all that but now it feels as if will I be stuck there.", "sender": "user", "created_at": "2026-10-17T06:53:38.202111+00:00", "sender_name": "Komal"}, {"id": "ef65e04b-b13e-42c4-9177-aa3aa2bfebd8", "text": "I have also gone through similar experiences in my life. There have been difficult times, moments when tears would well up in my eyes, too.\\nBut with time, I realised something beautiful, look at how beautifully those very experiences have shaped me!\\n\\nThink of a sculptor carving a murti. With every tak-tak of the chisel, the stone undergoes force and pain. But when the carving is complete, the murti looks incredibly beautiful.\\nSimilarly, the Universe sends different situations into our lives. Each situation chisels us, shapes us, and helps us become a better version of ourselves.\\n\\nSo, whenever you go through difficult times, don't just look at the pain you are experiencing. Look at the person you are becoming through it. Consider it a boon from the Universe. Perhaps, through every challenge, the Universe is simply chiselling you into something even more beautiful.\\n\\n        ~ Muniraj Shri MuktiMandan Vijayji MS", "sender": "admin", "created_at": "2026-10-28T04:43:50.721012+00:00", "sender_name": "ILJ Mentor"}]	2026-10-28 04:43:50.721012+00
